> Keep in mind, you can "rust"proof *any* piece of armor (cloak, helmet, 
> shield, etc.), not just your suit; this will fireproof, rotproof, or 
> corrodeproof things that cannot rust. Also, rustproofing mithril or 
> dragon scale mail is a waste, as neither can be rusted, corroded, 
> burned, or rotted.

This is a matter of semantics.  Some materials are subject to damage and
sme are not.  All objects have a flag in their data structure to mark
them fixed or proofed.  If you go through the process on an item that is
immune to damage does that have no effect?  If the data structure is
changed and the object is eventually polymorphed into a material that is
subject to damage it comes out of the polymorph fixed.  Obscure
difference ;^)


